  "voice_and_collaboration": "I performed the Persian voices, often changing them with effects. Number 5 teaches a ninth-grade Work and Technology lesson; number 6 uses several character voices; number 7 includes my performance of a girl's narration. English on-screen text is visible in parts of 7 and 8, but this archive does not claim complete subtitles in 18 languages. My twin brother Armiya plays Herobrine in 9 and joins the characters in 11.",
  "missing_work": "Some earlier work, my eighth-grade experiments and part of the planned school-story sequel were not retained. They cannot be included or reconstructed here. The coordinates project was made for a Khwarizmi competition, but it was not submitted before the deadline; it is not presented as a competition entry or award. These exports belong to the path that led toward my book and later 3D work.",
